---
import VisaPage from '../../../components/ui/VisaPage.astro';
---
<VisaPage
  lang="en"
  title="Panama Qualified Investor Visa — Golden Visa"
  description="Complete guide to Panama's Qualified Investor Visa (Golden Visa): three investment routes, fast-track 30–45 day processing, remote application and Special Passport."
  visaName="Panama Qualified Investor Visa"
  tag="Golden Visa · Investors"
  tagColor="bg-gold/30 text-slate font-bold"
  mainReq="Qualifying investment in Panama"
  investment="From $300,000 (real estate) · $500,000 (stocks) · $750,000 (fixed deposit)"
  processingTime="30–45 days (fast-track)"
  renewalNote="Permanent from first application · investment held min. 5 years"
  intro="Panama's Golden Visa — permanent residency in exchange for a qualifying investment in the country. The fastest and most flexible pathway to permanent residency available in Panama, with three investment options and the unique ability to process the entire application remotely via power of attorney, before you ever set foot in Panama. Residency is approved in 30 to 45 days through a priority window at the Servicio Nacional de Migración."
  requirements={[
    "Option A — Real estate: minimum $300,000 USD investment in titled real estate registered in the Public Registry of Panama. Multiple properties may be combined to reach the threshold; investment can be held personally or through a corporate structure where you are the ultimate beneficial owner",
    "Option B — Stock market: minimum $500,000 USD in securities authorized for purchase through a licensed broker-dealer (Casa de Valores) regulated in Panama",
    "Option C — Fixed-term bank deposit: minimum $750,000 USD in a fixed-term deposit at any bank holding a General License regulated by the Superintendency of Banks of Panama",
    "Investment must be maintained for a minimum of 5 years from the date of residency approval",
    "Valid passport with at least 6 months of validity remaining, plus complete authenticated copies",
    "Apostilled criminal background check from country of origin — maximum 6 months old",
    "Declaration of lawful origin of funds (source of funds documentation)",
    "Apostilled civil documents: birth certificate; marriage certificate if applicable",
    "Medical exam in Panama (can be deferred to first physical visit)",
    "Power of attorney (apostilled) to your Panamanian attorney for remote filing — the entire process up to the moment of arrival can be done without entering Panama",
    "All foreign documents must be apostilled and translated by an Authorized Public Translator in Panama"
  ]}
  benefits={[
    "Permanent residency approved in 30 to 45 days via priority processing window — the fastest permanent residency in Panama",
    "Entire pre-approval process can be handled remotely via power of attorney — no need to travel to Panama during the application phase",
    "Permanent residency from the first application — no renewals, no expiration",
    "No restrictions on working in Panama — full labor rights with no employment quota limitations",
    "Freedom to open companies, bank accounts, and operate commercially in Panama without restrictions",
    "Spouse and children automatically qualify as dependents",
    "Panama taxes only Panama-source income — foreign-source income from your investment or business activities outside Panama is not taxed in Panama",
    "Option to apply for the Special Panamanian Passport (Documento Especial de Viaje) — travel to 140+ countries without a visa, including the entire Schengen Area and the United Kingdom",
    "Compatible with the naturalization process: Panamanian citizenship may be applied for after 5 years of permanent residency"
  ]}
  notFor={[
    "You do not have at least $300,000 USD in investable capital for the real estate route, or the higher thresholds for stocks or fixed deposits",
    "You are not prepared to keep your investment in Panama for a minimum of 5 years",
    "You prefer not to lock up capital — the Friendly Nations visa may offer more flexibility if you meet the eligibility criteria",
    "You need work authorization but not residency — explore the Friendly Nations visa with the labor route instead"
  ]}
  faqs={[
    {
      q: "What are the three investment options for Panama's Qualified Investor Visa?",
      a: "There are three qualifying routes: (1) Real estate — a minimum $300,000 USD investment in titled real estate in Panama's Public Registry. Multiple properties can be combined, and the investment can be held personally or through a corporate structure. (2) Stock market — a minimum $500,000 USD in securities purchased through a licensed Panama broker-dealer. (3) Fixed-term bank deposit — a minimum $750,000 USD in a term deposit at any bank with a General License regulated by the Superintendency of Banks of Panama. The investment must be maintained for a minimum of 5 years."
    },
    {
      q: "How fast is the Panama Qualified Investor Visa processed?",
      a: "The Qualified Investor Visa is processed through a priority investment window at the Servicio Nacional de Migración, with residency typically approved in 30 to 45 days. This makes it by far the fastest permanent residency pathway available in Panama. The process is also unique in that the entire application — from opening the investment to submitting the file — can be completed remotely via an apostilled power of attorney granted to a Panamanian attorney, with no need to be physically present in Panama until you are ready to collect your permanent resident card."
    },
    {
      q: "Can I process the Panama Golden Visa application without traveling to Panama?",
      a: "Yes — this is one of the most distinctive features of the Qualified Investor Visa. The entire application process, from setting up the investment to filing the residency petition, can be handled remotely through an apostilled power of attorney granted to your Panamanian immigration attorney. You only need to travel to Panama once: to have your photograph taken for the permanent resident card and to pick up your cédula (Panama national identity card for residents). The process has no requirement for a prior visit to Panama."
    },
    {
      q: "What is the Special Panamanian Passport and am I eligible?",
      a: "The Special Panamanian Passport (Documento Especial de Viaje) is a travel document issued by the Panamanian government to qualifying residents. It provides visa-free or visa-on-arrival access to more than 140 countries, including all 27 Schengen Area countries and the United Kingdom. It does not confer Panamanian nationality or political rights — your original citizenship remains unchanged. Holders of the Qualified Investor Visa are among those eligible to apply for this passport, along with their dependents. It is an optional benefit, not automatic."
    },
    {
      q: "Can family members be included in a Qualified Investor Visa application?",
      a: "Yes. A spouse and minor children can be included as dependents in the same application. Dependents do not need to make a separate investment — they benefit from the qualifying investment of the main applicant. Parents of the main applicant and children up to age 25 (if single, full-time students, and economically dependent) may also qualify as dependents. Each dependent incurs an additional professional fee."
    }
  ]}
>
  <div class="my-8 p-5 rounded-2xl bg-coral/10 border border-coral/20">
    <p class="font-semibold text-slate mb-2">⚡ Investment threshold update</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-mid">Panama's National Migration Service has periodically adjusted the minimum investment thresholds for this category. Always verify current requirements with a qualified immigration attorney before initiating any investment specifically for this visa — the amounts above reflect the most recent available data as of mid-2026.</p>
  </div>
</VisaPage>
